}
},
"autoHeight": false,
"components": ["2cc43715-13b0-4cad-92d7-5b4f61fe66a7"],
"content": "<p>I love sophisticated games.</p>",
"height": 281.0,
"outputs": ["e3a5e255-f263-4e25-830d-1b352aa4e48a", "4e802d85-167a-450e-b22d-6e57b6dbffd8"],
"theme": "default",
"title": null,
"width": 301.0,
"x": 5480.0,
"y": 4160.0
},
"df0f7a18-bacf-4c1d-9cc6-3ab4487615fe": {
"autoHeight": true,
"components": [],
"content": "<p>To export your project for Godot, go to:</p><blockquote><p>Export > Engine > Export for Godot</p></blockquote><p>This will download the project's data as two .gd (GDScript) files, compressed in one .zip file.</p><p>Unzip and drag those files into the Godot project folder, at <strong>res://addons/arcweave</strong>, which is where the Arcweave plugin exists in your project.</p>",
"height": 279.0,
"outputs": ["9366f063-e439-4dd0-9066-e90ef608b088"],
"theme": "lightBlue",
"title": "<p>Export for Godot</p>",
"width": 381.0,
"x": 9940.0,
"y": 11540.0
},
"dfbf38a3-9c77-4ef0-869a-7ef8e0704468": {
"assets": {
"cover": {
