},
"name": "Regrets",
"notes": {
"0caefa33-1954-4049-bbca-7f938067f124": {
"autoHeight": true,
"content": "<p>The <strong>STOP</strong> component gives Godot the information that the dialogue sequence ends here.</p>",
"height": 101.0,
"theme": "pink",
"width": 301.0,
"x": 4280.0,
"y": 2620.0
},
"1f6bc6a8-314d-47de-9485-e6bdf5af56c2": {
"autoHeight": true,
"content": "<p>While the dialogue is over for the game engine, Arcweave sends the flow to the <strong>Map</strong> board, where the rooms are noted.</p>",
"height": 112.0,
"theme": "blue",
"width": 301.0,
"x": 6140.0,
"y": 2580.0
},
"2e108806-8040-4c22-813a-c5d1816584cb": {
"content": "<p>Any i_item state:</p><p><strong>0</strong>: nowhere<br><strong>1</strong>: initial position / before been taken<br><strong>2</strong>: taken by the player<br><strong>3</strong>: used/gone</p><p>Note all objects start in play; some start out of play (nowhere).</p>",
"height": 223.0,
"theme": "lightBlue",
"width": 301.0,
"x": 2860.0,
"y": 7140.0
},
"2e16a59f-c03f-4287-a296-7e0cec8499b9": {
"autoHeight": false,
"content": "<p><strong>ACTIVITIES: INVENTORY ADD/REMOVE</strong></p><p>Activity components, like <span class=\"mention mention-component\" data-id=\"ce5d1948-6893-44ef-845c-e81c48926efc\" data-type=\"component\" data-label=\"INVENTORY: ADD\">INVENTORY: ADD</span> and <span class=\"mention mention-component\" data-id=\"2936dbdb-7639-4d36-b6a3-c9ee79df168a\" data-type=\"component\" data-label=\"INVENTORY: REMOVE\">INVENTORY: REMOVE</span> inform the game engine that a change must occur regarding the player's possessions, with the other item components (here: the <span class=\"mention mention-component\" data-id=\"7dc10d72-cac3-475e-9076-5c984e2884b0\" data-type=\"component\" data-label=\"key\">key</span>) getting added or removed.</p>",
"height": 221.0,
"theme": "pink",
"width": 301.0,
"x": 8140.0,
"y": 1960.0
},
"3220f565-1eae-45e4-97a5-079ece22a793": {
"autoHeight": true,
"content": "<p><strong>ACTIVITIES: INVENTORY ADD/REMOVE</strong></p><p>Activity components, like <span class=\"mention mention-component\" data-id=\"ce5d1948-6893-44ef-845c-e81c48926efc\" data-type=\"component\" data-label=\"INVENTORY: ADD\">INVENTORY: ADD</span> and <span class=\"mention mention-component\" data-id=\"2936dbdb-7639-4d36-b6a3-c9ee79df168a\" data-type=\"component\" data-label=\"INVENTORY: REMOVE\">INVENTORY: REMOVE</span> inform the game engine that a change must occur regarding the player's possessions, with the other item components (here: the <span class=\"mention mention-component\" data-id=\"d95da3c0-0c71-47bd-9d40-d909dbfaaeef\" data-type=\"component\" data-label=\"Amstrad 6128\">Amstrad 6128</span>) getting added or removed.</p>",
"height": 232.0,
"theme": "pink",
"width": 301.0,
"x": 3180.0,
"y": 7260.0
},
"4135d03e-e053-4b54-9165-925da8b7a5ed": {
"autoHeight": true,
"content": "<p>When the game engine encounters a <span class=\"mention mention-component\" data-id=\"9394ffb5-bf06-4b15-b02c-3123b1b05067\" data-type=\"component\" data-label=\"FOLLOW RANDOM OUTPUT\">FOLLOW RANDOM OUTPUT</span> component attached to the current element, it sends the flow to one of the element's outputs in random.</p><p>(Of course, this doesn't work in Arcweave's Play Mode, where all outputs will simply appear as options.)</p>",
"height": 211.0,
"theme": "pink",
"width": 301.0,
"x": 13660.0,
"y": 10840.0
},
"41b28eb9-26a0-4cd0-b6c6-c1922947a3d0": {
"autoHeight": true,
"content": "<p><strong>BOTTLENECKS</strong></p><p>To make controlling the dialogue flow easier, we have created 4 bottleneck points. These have the following 3 functions:</p><p>• they make sure the branching dialogue rejoins the flow (the definition of a bottleneck)</p><p>• they allow loops where different options can be tried.</p><p>• they work as points of no return: once you pass e.g. Bottleneck 3, the next time you talk to Andreas, you can continue the dialogue from Bottleneck 3 or later.</p>",
"height": 424.0,
"theme": "pink",
"width": 261.0,
"x": 8880.0,
"y": 5340.0
},
"494229c4-4c0b-4d3e-b405-7aa0cd8c6f3b": {
"autoHeight": true,
"content": "<p><strong>ACTIVITIES: INVENTORY ADD/REMOVE</strong></p><p>Activity components, like <span class=\"mention mention-component\" data-id=\"ce5d1948-6893-44ef-845c-e81c48926efc\" data-type=\"component\" data-label=\"INVENTORY: ADD\">INVENTORY: ADD</span> and <span class=\"mention mention-component\" data-id=\"2936dbdb-7639-4d36-b6a3-c9ee79df168a\" data-type=\"component\" data-label=\"INVENTORY: REMOVE\">INVENTORY: REMOVE</span> inform the game engine that a change must occur regarding the player's possessions, with the other item components (here: the <span class=\"mention mention-component\" data-id=\"d95da3c0-0c71-47bd-9d40-d909dbfaaeef\" data-type=\"component\" data-label=\"Amstrad 6128\">Amstrad 6128</span>) getting added or removed.</p>",
"height": 232.0,
"theme": "pink",
"width": 301.0,
"x": 3560.0,
"y": 7020.0
},
"4a1f36cb-5df3-45ba-8bd3-887c019d974b": {
"autoHeight": true,
"content": "<p>Those 3 elements are only used by Arcweave's Play Mode.</p><p>The game engine uses the elements in the <span class=\"mention mention-board\" data-id=\"e346ed24-8a00-4176-be50-92e02e99b9e6\" data-type=\"board\" data-label=\"Player Actions\">Player Actions</span> board, which direct the flow to the same jumpers.</p><p>This repetition is a convention so that both systems work: the Play Mode and the game engine.</p>",
"height": 226.0,
"theme": "purple",
"width": 301.0,
"x": 6140.0,
"y": 1760.0
},
"580e4d95-e8ad-4da6-979a-b0c6889d0ee1": {
"autoHeight": true,
"content": "<p><strong>TALK TO ANDREAS</strong></p><p>Since <span class=\"mention mention-component\" data-id=\"2d1e3aaa-d1a3-4565-a540-c0fb9853e2cf\" data-type=\"component\" data-label=\"Andreas\">Andreas</span> is our NPC, he has the largest dialogue tree. Dialogue with him starts from this element, but soon branches out to various boards.</p><p>Note that the game engine searches for the starting element for the action TALK TO ANDREAS in the <span class=\"mention mention-board\" data-id=\"e346ed24-8a00-4176-be50-92e02e99b9e6\" data-type=\"board\" data-label=\"Player Actions\">Player Actions</span> board.</p>",
"height": 247.0,
"theme": "blue",
"width": 301.0,
"x": 4760.0,
"y": 4920.0
},
"5d8f06fc-f994-484c-b9e7-4df6ee5c3fa0": {
"autoHeight": true,
"content": "<p>When the game engine encounters a <span class=\"mention mention-component\" data-id=\"9394ffb5-bf06-4b15-b02c-3123b1b05067\" data-type=\"component\" data-label=\"FOLLOW RANDOM OUTPUT\">FOLLOW RANDOM OUTPUT</span> component attached to the current element, it sends the flow to one of the element's outputs in random.</p><p>(Of course, this doesn't work in Arcweave's Play Mode, where all outputs will simply appear as options.)</p>",
"height": 211.0,
"theme": "pink",
"width": 301.0,
"x": 9340.0,
"y": 12240.0
},
"6070a26a-5b39-4718-9b50-42667ec29332": {
"autoHeight": true,
"content": "<p>Yep, this is the next element.</p>",
"height": 101.0,
"theme": "blue",
"width": 301.0,
"x": 2480.0,
"y": 2680.0
},
"6509bb43-1c99-4588-8262-a4266e4c690f": {
"autoHeight": true,
"content": "<p>Arcscript takes care of the math, here, with function <strong>roll(n, m)</strong> generating a random number from 1 to 100 for each player.</p>",
"height": 101.0,
"theme": "pink",
"width": 681.0,
"x": 7460.0,
"y": 4260.0
},
"67e12be9-0276-4f10-90ee-c6caf21f30e9": {
"autoHeight": true,
"content": "<p>The <span class=\"mention mention-component\" data-id=\"a76b1b28-2731-4b50-a428-2a72c5d2b125\" data-type=\"component\" data-label=\"PAUSE\">PAUSE</span> component creates a pause after delivering the current element's content.</p><p>(The pause's length is set in the game engine, of course.)</p>",
"height": 148.0,
"theme": "pink",
"width": 301.0,
"x": 3500.0,
"y": 2620.0
},
"6ee9c825-fc1c-42f9-89ac-4750456403e5": {
"autoHeight": true,
"content": "<p>If an element looks as if it isn't coming from anywhere, search its title and you'll probably find a jumper leading to it—mystery solved.</p>",
"height": 112.0,
"theme": "lightBlue",
"width": 301.0,
"x": 3420.0,
"y": 4200.0
},
"71d64596-2185-4bef-8ed4-636239e0bfba": {
"autoHeight": true,
"content": "<p>Since all other options are conditioned, safety requires we add a fallback option, so there is always something to say.</p>",
"height": 101.0,
"theme": "lightBlue",
"width": 322.0,
"x": 5060.0,
"y": 8620.0
},
"72879444-d9d4-400a-b1f8-f30ee7717109": {
"autoHeight": true,
"content": "<p><strong>INTRO &amp; FINALE</strong></p><p>This board contains the game's Intro Sequence, as well as the Finale Sequence. Duh.</p>",
"height": 127.0,
"theme": "blue",
"width": 301.0,
"x": 1620.0,
"y": 2300.0
},
"737086d1-bbae-4ff9-ba0b-181bf108b6fe": {
"autoHeight": true,
"content": "<p>We use an audio component to play a sound effect over a specific dialogue line, like the <span class=\"mention mention-component\" data-id=\"270833c2-3f2d-41c6-adc5-f6436e2869b0\" data-type=\"component\" data-label=\"joke drum break\">joke drum break</span>, here.</p>",
"height": 101.0,
"theme": "pink",
"width": 301.0,
"x": 2320.0,
"y": 2240.0
},
"807f5ccf-7baa-4c3d-86ac-39a4a2d5bd58": {
"autoHeight": true,
"content": "<p><strong>ACTIVITIES: INVENTORY ADD/REMOVE</strong></p><p>Activity components, like <span class=\"mention mention-component\" data-id=\"ce5d1948-6893-44ef-845c-e81c48926efc\" data-type=\"component\" data-label=\"INVENTORY: ADD\">INVENTORY: ADD</span> and <span class=\"mention mention-component\" data-id=\"2936dbdb-7639-4d36-b6a3-c9ee79df168a\" data-type=\"component\" data-label=\"INVENTORY: REMOVE\">INVENTORY: REMOVE</span> inform the game engine that a change must occur regarding the player's possessions, with the other item components (here: the <span class=\"mention mention-component\" data-id=\"a4412312-b5d7-4826-8335-b51291c6e817\" data-type=\"component\" data-label=\"games magazines\">games magazines</span>) getting added or removed.</p>",
"height": 232.0,
"theme": "pink",
"width": 301.0,
"x": 1880.0,
"y": 3220.0
},
"84699a0a-1da4-4683-812a-2f2ec368d5b7": {
"autoHeight": true,
"content": "<p><strong>GIVE SOMETHING TO ANDREAS</strong></p><p>To keep this action separate, we have created a board for all the dialogue resulting from trying to give an item to <span class=\"mention mention-component\" data-id=\"2d1e3aaa-d1a3-4565-a540-c0fb9853e2cf\" data-type=\"component\" data-label=\"Andreas\">Andreas</span>.</p>",
"height": 148.0,
"theme": "blue",
"width": 301.0,
"x": 1080.0,
"y": 8220.0
},
"8996ff56-8856-4085-89ad-e105e8fa78f9": {
"autoHeight": true,
"content": "<p><strong>ACTIVITIES: INVENTORY ADD/REMOVE</strong></p><p>Activity components, like <span class=\"mention mention-component\" data-id=\"ce5d1948-6893-44ef-845c-e81c48926efc\" data-type=\"component\" data-label=\"INVENTORY: ADD\">INVENTORY: ADD</span> and <span class=\"mention mention-component\" data-id=\"2936dbdb-7639-4d36-b6a3-c9ee79df168a\" data-type=\"component\" data-label=\"INVENTORY: REMOVE\">INVENTORY: REMOVE</span> inform the game engine that a change must occur regarding the player's possessions, with the other item components (here: the <span class=\"mention mention-component\" data-id=\"a4412312-b5d7-4826-8335-b51291c6e817\" data-type=\"component\" data-label=\"games magazines\">games magazines</span>) getting added or removed.</p>",
"height": 232.0,
"theme": "pink",
"width": 301.0,
"x": 5420.0,
"y": 8120.0
},
"8a607ca9-ae75-4147-af25-6dd81335969b": {
"autoHeight": true,
"content": "<p>The component <span class=\"mention mention-component\" data-id=\"1ff6f2bd-7675-4f5e-958e-3d6ca5f102c2\" data-type=\"component\" data-label=\"OVERLAP NEXT\">OVERLAP NEXT</span> tells the game engine that the current content is not to be immediately rendered, but saved to be rendered along with that of the next element.</p><p>(This allows the content of only 2 elements to overlap, but the engine code could be altered to allow more.)</p>",
"height": 211.0,
"theme": "pink",
"width": 301.0,
"x": 7460.0,
"y": 4740.0
},
"8a94fa2d-44f9-47df-8f89-f8de04a084ea": {
"autoHeight": true,
"content": "<p><strong>BOTTLENECK AS LOOP</strong></p><p>This is an example where the bottleneck system is used to create a loop: the player is sent back to the same bottleneck, where they can pick another reply.</p>",
"height": 127.0,
"theme": "pink",
"width": 441.0,
"x": 8220.0,
"y": 7100.0
},
"8dbfd679-484e-4778-8fe4-7f4f5e15c047": {
"autoHeight": true,
"content": "<p><strong>ACTIVITIES: INVENTORY ADD/REMOVE</strong></p><p>Activity components, like <span class=\"mention mention-component\" data-id=\"ce5d1948-6893-44ef-845c-e81c48926efc\" data-type=\"component\" data-label=\"INVENTORY: ADD\">INVENTORY: ADD</span> and <span class=\"mention mention-component\" data-id=\"2936dbdb-7639-4d36-b6a3-c9ee79df168a\" data-type=\"component\" data-label=\"INVENTORY: REMOVE\">INVENTORY: REMOVE</span> inform the game engine that a change must occur regarding the player's possessions, with the other item components (here: the <span class=\"mention mention-component\" data-id=\"033582a9-c2ea-4fb5-97d9-f252d1303850\" data-type=\"component\" data-label=\"adventure game scripts\">adventure game scripts</span>) getting added or removed.</p>",
"height": 232.0,
"theme": "pink",
"width": 301.0,
"x": 1580.0,
"y": 4540.0
},
"934cb014-7e49-4e59-bb53-3e3a7f7e72c8": {
"autoHeight": true,
"content": "<p><strong>OBJECTS' RESPONSES</strong></p><p>This board has the dialogue trees for various player actions, like EXAMINE GAMES MAGAZINES.</p><p>Note that the game engine looks up the starting elements for those actions in the <span class=\"mention mention-board\" data-id=\"e346ed24-8a00-4176-be50-92e02e99b9e6\" data-type=\"board\" data-label=\"Player Actions\">Player Actions</span> board.</p>",
"height": 205.0,
"theme": "blue",
"width": 301.0,
"x": 1480.0,
"y": 1920.0
},
"9e9c40b7-d690-4ef2-955b-5732edba0d82": {
"autoHeight": false,
"content": "<p><strong>Any i_item states</strong>:</p><p><strong>0</strong>: nowhere / out of play<br><strong>1</strong>: initial position / before been taken<br><strong>2</strong>: taken by the player<br><strong>3</strong>: used/gone</p><p>Not all objects start in play; some start out of play.</p>",
"height": 221.0,
"theme": "lightBlue",
"width": 1441.0,
"x": 8640.0,
"y": 9700.0
},
"be40a917-6e8b-498e-a1b8-d8722ef46aba": {
"autoHeight": true,
"content": "<p>Godot runs this intro dialogue sequence automatically, since the method <strong>story.getCurrentElement()</strong> gets the project's starting element.</p><p>One detail: the game doesn't render this first element, but actually uses <strong>story.getCurrentOptions()</strong> to render the next element.</p>",
"height": 211.0,
"theme": "blue",
"width": 301.0,
"x": 1960.0,
"y": 2120.0
},
"c5f17f7e-9b3b-4b83-a5df-2230e7dd9dbf": {
"autoHeight": false,
"content": "<p>Any i_item state:</p><p><strong>0</strong>: nowhere<br><strong>1</strong>: initial position / before been taken<br><strong>2</strong>: taken by the player<br><strong>3</strong>: used/gone</p><p>Not all objects start in play; some start out of play (nowhere).</p>",
"height": 381.0,
"theme": "lightBlue",
"width": 301.0,
"x": 3980.0,
"y": 7160.0
},
"c63dca7c-4f09-4fd1-990c-746dbf6fb970": {
"autoHeight": true,
"content": "<p><strong>BOTTLENECK AS LOOP</strong></p><p>This is an example where the bottleneck system is used to create a loop: the player is sent back to the same bottleneck, where they can pick another reply.</p>",
"height": 127.0,
"theme": "pink",
"width": 441.0,
"x": 6840.0,
"y": 7460.0
},
"d0488c57-32c2-43fc-9ff3-86020c36d471": {
"autoHeight": true,
"content": "<p>You can read this Read Me as a diagram or right-click this element and choose <strong>Quickstart Play Mode from here</strong>, to read it on the Play Mode.</p>",
"height": 112.0,
"theme": "pink",
"width": 301.0,
"x": 10500.0,
"y": 10120.0
},
"d4558016-1b56-4939-8e5f-9b4bf8ad6df8": {
"autoHeight": true,
"content": "<p>This element does not interest the game engine. It contains a simulation for the objects the player can interact with, so the Play Mode prototype can reproduce the closest experience to the point and click UI possible.</p>",
"height": 154.0,
"theme": "blue",
"width": 301.0,
"x": 10660.0,
"y": 11520.0
},
"d7375fc1-1f43-4bba-ac4d-5451a2095804": {
"autoHeight": true,
"content": "<p>The <span class=\"mention mention-component\" data-id=\"c39bbc27-aa0e-4753-9c59-b2b8ab31384e\" data-type=\"component\" data-label=\"TITLE\">TITLE</span> component informs the game engine this element's content will not be a spoken line but a title.</p>",
"height": 101.0,
"theme": "orange",
"width": 301.0,
"x": 6160.0,
"y": 2700.0
},
"da041e96-3ebf-4e77-bc1d-d44f31264281": {
"autoHeight": true,
"content": "<p>The <span class=\"mention mention-component\" data-id=\"78398b84-0d0b-4038-9f72-44b2459435a2\" data-type=\"component\" data-label=\"EXIT THROUGH EXIT\">EXIT THROUGH EXIT</span> component tells the game engine the room must change, as if the player walked through the attached exit (here: the <span class=\"mention mention-component\" data-id=\"74a88987-534b-44c6-8434-22ea6de90349\" data-type=\"component\" data-label=\"final exit\">final exit</span> component).</p>",
"height": 133.0,
"theme": "pink",
"width": 301.0,
"x": 11160.0,
"y": 13700.0
},
"f8e1172e-ab6e-4a9d-b710-49e0ef2b536a": {
"autoHeight": true,
"content": "<p>This element does not interest the game engine. It contains a simulation for the objects the player can interact with, so the Play Mode prototype can reproduce the closest experience to the point and click UI possible.</p>",
"height": 154.0,
"theme": "blue",
"width": 301.0,
"x": 10740.0,
"y": 9760.0
},
"fe238a51-75c3-4c93-9a5c-0e5d2c945e65": {
"autoHeight": true,
"content": "<p><strong>NAVIGATION MAP</strong></p><p>This board simulates the navigation among the game's rooms (here only two).</p>",
"height": 106.0,
"theme": "blue",
"width": 421.0,
"x": 10320.0,
"y": 9560.0
},
"ff22480a-3405-4e36-96b3-f33a9e26b999": {
"autoHeight": true,
"content": "<p><strong>PLAYER ACTIONS</strong></p><p>This board contains all the elements springing from a VERB + OBJECT combination (e.g. EXAMINE MAGAZINES) or an OBJECT + OBJECT combination (e.g. GIVE AMSTRAD TO ANDREAS).</p><p><strong><em>The combinations are signified by the relevant attached components.</em></strong></p><p>If some specific combinations are missing (e.g. USE AMSTRAD WITH PIANO), the game will look up at some <strong>generic replies</strong> blocking the action (e.g. USE GENERIC WITH GENERIC --> \"This doesn't seem to work.\" or EXAMINE GENERIC --> \"You don't see anything special about that.\") There is a <span class=\"mention mention-component\" data-id=\"95d2c620-df08-4996-b9a3-0011e69ae8ba\" data-type=\"component\" data-label=\"GENERIC REPLY ITEM\">GENERIC REPLY ITEM</span> component created for this purpose.</p><p>In most cases, all those starting elements point to a jumper, leading the flow to another board (like <span class=\"mention mention-board\" data-id=\"33921d60-74db-4a1f-8e49-21b8b9547d52\" data-type=\"board\" data-label=\"Object Responses\">Object Responses</span> or <span class=\"mention mention-board\" data-id=\"9b928a67-67a8-40d4-ae86-e6275c091e88\" data-type=\"board\" data-label=\"Andreas DIAL 1\">Andreas DIAL 1</span>), containing the dialogue tree for the occasion. In cases of very short replies (as with EXAMINE ANDREAS), their elements are included here for simplicity.</p>",
"height": 382.0,
"theme": "blue",
"width": 621.0,
"x": 9980.0,
"y": 9780.0
}
},
"startingElement": "7bcc5363-e1f2-4491-8471-f36f3190a843",
